1
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:05,640
- Okay, well, make yourself at home.
- Okay.

2
00:00:05,804 --> 00:00:09,264
(Penny:)- Thank you.
- You're very welcome.

3
00:00:10,141 --> 00:00:12,101
[MOUTHS]
You're very welcome.

4
00:00:12,602 --> 00:00:15,392
(Penny:)This looks like some serious stuff.
Leonard, did you do this?

5
00:00:15,563 --> 00:00:17,983
(Sheldon:)Actually, that's my work.

6
00:00:18,525 --> 00:00:19,525
(Penny:)Wow.

7
00:00:19,692 --> 00:00:22,112
(Sheldon:)Yeah, well, it's just some
quantum mechanics...

8
00:00:22,278 --> 00:00:26,118
(Sheldon:)...with a little string theory doodling
around the edges. That part's just a joke.

9
00:00:26,282 --> 00:00:29,492
It's a spoof of the Born-Oppenheimer
approximation.

10
00:00:30,412 --> 00:00:33,912
(Penny:)So you're, like, one of those
Beautiful Mind genius guys.

11
00:00:34,999 --> 00:00:36,499
(Sheldon:)Yeah.

12
00:00:37,502 --> 00:00:38,752
(Penny:)This is really impressive.

13
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:42,170
(Leonard:)I have a board, if you like boards.
This is my board.

14
00:00:42,924 --> 00:00:44,304
(Penny:)Holy smokes.

15
00:00:44,467 --> 00:00:47,757
If by "holy smokes," you mean
a derivative restatement of the stuff...

16
00:00:47,929 --> 00:00:51,309
(Sheldon:)...you can find scribbled on the wall
of any men's room at MIT, sure.

17
00:00:51,891 --> 00:00:53,311
(Penny:)- What?
- Oh, come on.

18
00:00:53,476 --> 00:00:57,106
(Sheldon:)Who hasn't seen this differential below
"here I sit brokenhearted"?

19
00:00:57,272 --> 00:01:01,312
At least I didn't have to invent 26
dimensions just to make the math come out.

